# Referral short links (/ref/:code) — handled by the ref-redirect Netlify Edge
# Function (netlify/edge-functions/ref-redirect.ts), NOT a rule in this file.
# History: a 200 rewrite here left the browser's visible URL at /ref/:code
# with no query string, so ref.html's client-side
# `URLSearchParams(location.search).get('code')` never saw the code and
# bounced to /index.html — fixed by switching to a 301 (2026-08-05). That
# plain 301 rule then dropped extra query params (utm_source, etc.) on the
# short link, because Netlify's redirect engine only auto-forwards the
# incoming query string when the "to" target has no query string of its
# own, and our target must always carry ?code= (#630, 2026-08-06). The edge
# function forwards every incoming param; see netlify.toml [[edge_functions]].
https://stellaredgeservices.com/* /stellar-edge.html 200
https://www.stellaredgeservices.com/* /stellar-edge.html 200

